% A web shop handles four personal data breaches. Under Article 33 of the
% GDPR it notifies the supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming
% aware of a breach, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk, and a
% later notice must give reasons; under Article 34 it also tells the people
% affected of a high risk, unless the data was encrypted (Article 34(3)(a)).
% Its hosting processor must alert it without undue delay, which their
% processing agreement sets at 24 hours (Article 33(2)).
% The shop breaches Article 33(1) by never notifying the ransomware attack,
% and Article 34(1) by not telling the people whose health data leaked; the
% processor breaches Article 33(2) by alerting the shop to that leak after 30
% hours. The risk levels are the shop's assessments, given as facts.
% Shows legal rules with exceptions as "it is not the case that", number
% comparisons, names written as definite phrases, and expected answers.
% Source https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 33 and 34)

the templates are:
    *a breach* is a personal data breach,
    *a breach* has *a level* risk,
    *a breach* is unlikely to result in a risk,
    *a breach* concerns encrypted data,
    the controller notified the authority of *a breach* after *a number* hours,
    the controller recorded the reasons for the delay of *a breach*,
    the controller informed the data subjects of *a breach*,
    the processor alerted the controller to *a breach* after *a number* hours,
    the processing agreement allows *a number* hours to alert the controller,
    *a breach* must be notified to the supervisory authority,
    *a breach* is notified in time,
    *a breach* is notified late,
    *a breach* must be communicated to the data subjects,
    *a party* breaches *an article* for *a breach*.

the knowledge base gdpr breach notification includes:

a breach is unlikely to result in a risk
    if the breach has low risk.

% Article 33(1): the controller notifies the supervisory authority of a
% personal data breach, unless it is unlikely to result in a risk.
a breach must be notified to the supervisory authority
    if the breach is a personal data breach
    and it is not the case that
        the breach is unlikely to result in a risk.

% Hours count from the moment the controller became aware of the breach.
a breach is notified in time
    if the controller notified the authority of the breach after a number N hours
    and N <= 72.

a breach is notified late
    if the controller notified the authority of the breach after a number N hours
    and N > 72.

% Article 34(1) and 34(3)(a): a high risk is communicated to the data
% subjects, unless the data was encrypted.
a breach must be communicated to the data subjects
    if the breach is a personal data breach
    and the breach has high risk
    and it is not the case that
        the breach concerns encrypted data.

the controller breaches "Article 33(1)" for a breach
    if the breach must be notified to the supervisory authority
    and it is not the case that
        the controller notified the authority of the breach after a number hours.

% A notice after 72 hours is lawful only with the reasons for the delay.
the controller breaches "Article 33(1)" for a breach
    if the breach is notified late
    and it is not the case that
        the controller recorded the reasons for the delay of the breach.

the controller breaches "Article 34(1)" for a breach
    if the breach must be communicated to the data subjects
    and it is not the case that
        the controller informed the data subjects of the breach.

% Article 33(2): the processor alerts the controller without undue delay.
the processor breaches "Article 33(2)" for a breach
    if the processor alerted the controller to the breach after a number N hours
    and the processing agreement allows a number M hours to alert the controller
    and N > M.

scenario web shop is:
    the lost laptop is a personal data breach.
    the lost laptop has high risk.
    the lost laptop concerns encrypted data.
    the controller notified the authority of the lost laptop after 40 hours.
    the database leak is a personal data breach.
    the database leak has high risk.
    the controller notified the authority of the database leak after 90 hours.
    the controller recorded the reasons for the delay of the database leak.
    the processor alerted the controller to the database leak after 30 hours.
    the ransomware attack is a personal data breach.
    the ransomware attack has moderate risk.
    the processor alerted the controller to the ransomware attack after 6 hours.
    the misdirected email is a personal data breach.
    the misdirected email has low risk.
    the processing agreement allows 24 hours to alert the controller.
    notify expects answers ["the lost laptop must be notified to the supervisory authority",
        "the database leak must be notified to the supervisory authority",
        "the ransomware attack must be notified to the supervisory authority"].
    timely expects answers ["the lost laptop is notified in time"].
    late expects answers ["the database leak is notified late"].
    communicate expects answers ["the database leak must be communicated to the data subjects"].
    breaches expects answers ["the controller breaches Article 33(1) for the ransomware attack",
        "the controller breaches Article 34(1) for the database leak",
        "the processor breaches Article 33(2) for the database leak"].

query notify is:
    which breach must be notified to the supervisory authority.

query timely is:
    which breach is notified in time.

query late is:
    which breach is notified late.

query communicate is:
    which breach must be communicated to the data subjects.

query breaches is:
    which party breaches which article for which breach.
